.TH LIGHTXR 8 "2026-10-21" "de-xr" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
lightxr \- display manager with a local and OpenXR login greeter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
lightxr [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A LightDM fork that authenticates through PAM and launches desktop sessions, including DomeD. Its native greeter (FLTK by default, Qt6 at build time) uses a separate OpenXR presenter. A privileged broker connects the greeter to already\-running trusted XR runtimes. Authentication remains in the display manager. Installation and service activation are separate operations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "\-\-config FILE"
Use the specified display\-manager configuration file.
.TP
.B "\-\-show\-config"
Show the merged configuration and exit.
.TP
.B "\-\-debug"
Print debugging messages.
.TP
.B "\-\-test\-mode"
Run unprivileged, skipping operations requiring root.
.TP
.B "\-\-pid\-file FILE"
Choose the PID file.
.TP
.B "\-\-log\-dir DIRECTORY"
Choose the log directory.
.TP
.B "\-\-run\-dir DIRECTORY"
Choose the runtime\-state directory.
.TP
.B "\-\-cache\-dir DIRECTORY"
Choose the cache directory.
.TP
.B "\-\-version"
Show version.
.TP
.B "\-\-help"
Show options.
.SH FILES
/etc/lightxr/lightdm.conf configures the display manager. /etc/lightxr/broker.json configures trusted XR server owners and runtime connections. /etc/pam.d/lightxr and /etc/pam.d/lightxr\-greeter define authentication policies. /run/lightxr\-broker/bridge.sock is the default broker socket.
.SH SERVICES
lightxr.service runs the display manager; lightxr\-broker.service runs the trusted\-runtime broker. Review the distribution\-specific PAM policy and installation guide before selecting LightXR as the next\-boot display manager.
.SH SEE ALSO
lightxr\-greeter(1), dome\-compositor(1), pam(8)
